Z||000008||Uaana||05-15-2000||03:24 PM||||As for the Firebird/Camaro brakes if I remember correctly the rotor diamter is too large to fit in the wheels or something like that. Although if you were using 16" rims I don't see why that would be a prob.... But with the standard 14/15 wheels I think the rotors were too large and something with the size of the caliper being too large to fit the mounting bracket. suppose you could have a custom mounting bracket made.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||05-15-2000||08:19 PM||||The Fiero Store sells a complete bolt on front vented brake kit that uses the Beretta brakes. My brother has it but it is not installed yet. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||BBBAD GT||05-16-2000||09:45 AM||||MM<P>I just went through the whole 88 GA brake swap, front and rear with the Blazer MC change too.  Best thing was all of the loaded calipers and rotors (all bendix parts) from Carparts.com with 30% off came to around $200 with core charges.  I'm happy with the swap, ton's better than what I had.  If you are ever in Southern IL, come on by and I'll show you what they feel like.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||05-16-2000||10:35 AM||||V-8 Archies kit uses F-body (camero/firebird) and Cadillac parts. Going to the larger rotors and calipers you cannot put anything smaller than a 16" wheel. Archies kit is a bolt on kit but I am not sure what the cost is.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||05-16-2000||11:10 AM||||Thanx, but I'd better stay with something that will allow 15" rims.  The Grape Ape currently has some nice ARE aftermarket (15") rims on it now and I'd kinda like to keep them on for a while.  Eventually I plan to upgrade to at least 16s and maybe 17s, but my budget just won't allow for that now.||||reg||1
